Trump, Xi, AI

Last week, the world freaked out about an AI apocalypse. Now the two most p=
owerful men, running the countries with the two most advanced AI industries=
, are going to discuss that possible doomsday. Donald Trump and Xi Jinping =
are set to greet one another on Wednesday and meet for talks in Washington =
DC, and artificial intelligence will be high on the agenda.

Though their meeting reflects concern for AI at the highest levels of gover=
nment, which is a generally positive sign, early indicators are not signall=
ing that either nation is willing to put regulatory checks on the technolog=
y. The US and Chinese leaders have stressed in recent days that a slowdown =
of AI development is unnecessary.

